WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.609
Soft Skill Playbook.

2
00:00:01.889 --> 00:00:03.361
From the Soft Skill Playbook.

3
00:00:05.111 --> 00:00:09.185
A 94-day English and communication course, one lesson a day.

4
00:00:09.465 --> 00:00:15.951
It starts with basic sentences and questions and ends with salary negotiation and the CEO review.

5
00:00:16.231 --> 00:00:28.817
Real conversations for the railway station, airport, restaurant, hospital, gym, yoga class, visa interview and many more everyday situations, then your manager, juniors, clients and CEO.

6
00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.021
Part 1.

7
00:00:31.301 --> 00:00:32.133
The course.

8
00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:34.279
Start here:

9
00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:35.647
Master Prompts:

10
00:00:35.927 --> 00:00:40.556
Copy the course tutor prompt into any AI assistant and type Start Day 1.

11
00:00:40.836 --> 00:00:44.292
It teaches, role-plays, quizzes and corrects you every day.

12
00:00:44.572 --> 00:00:46.385
Phase 1, English Basics:

13
00:00:46.665 --> 00:00:48.031
Days 1 to 15.

14
00:00:48.311 --> 00:00:57.548
Sentences, yes or no and wh- questions, answers, tenses, polite English, numbers, phrasal verbs, pronunciation and common mistakes.

15
00:00:57.828 --> 00:00:59.535
Phase 2, Communication:

16
00:00:59.815 --> 00:01:01.521
Days 16 to 24.

17
00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:10.121
Point-first communication, listening, feedback, confidence, public speaking, storytelling, small talk, phone calls and negotiation.

18
00:01:10.401 --> 00:01:12.151
Phase 3, Everyday Life:

19
00:01:12.431 --> 00:01:14.308
Days 25 to 58.

20
00:01:14.588 --> 00:01:23.953
Train, metro, visa, flight, hotel, restaurant, grocery, bank locker, insurance, hospital, gym, yoga, salon, police, school, landlord and more.

21
00:01:25.303 --> 00:01:26.690
Phase 4, Workplace:

22
00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.805
Days 59 to 78.

23
00:01:29.085 --> 00:01:39.730
Stand-ups, email, time management, docs, problem solving, manager, juniors, CEO, clients, difficult conversations, remote work, mentoring and team events.

24
00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:41.290
Phase 5, Career:

25
00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:43.490
Days 79 to 94.

26
00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:54.223
Career planning, resume, cover letter, LinkedIn, job hunting, interviews, reviews, promotion, appraisal, salary, resignation, layoffs, burnout and graduation.

27
00:01:55.573 --> 00:01:56.448
Part 2.

28
00:01:56.728 --> 00:01:57.987
How each day works.

29
00:01:59.237 --> 00:02:00.154
Step 1:

30
00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:04.615
Learn: key words, the sentence or question pattern, examples (10 min).

31
00:02:04.895 --> 00:02:05.813
Step 2:

32
00:02:06.093 --> 00:02:09.847
Read aloud: play both roles in the conversations (5 min).

33
00:02:10.127 --> 00:02:11.045
Step 3:

34
00:02:11.325 --> 00:02:14.866
Practise: exercises with answers you can check (5 min).

35
00:02:15.146 --> 00:02:16.106
Step 4:

36
00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:19.799
Role-play: run the same day with the AI tutor (10 min).

37
00:02:20.079 --> 00:02:21.039
Step 5:

38
00:02:21.319 --> 00:02:25.266
Use it: say one new sentence in real life today, then tick Done.

39
00:02:26.616 --> 00:02:27.512
Part 3.

40
00:02:27.792 --> 00:02:29.008
Where should I start?

41
00:02:30.258 --> 00:02:31.666
New to speaking English:

42
00:02:31.946 --> 00:02:33.909
Start at Day 1 and go in order.

43
00:02:34.189 --> 00:02:37.538
Don't skip Phase 1, because everything after it builds on it.

44
00:02:37.818 --> 00:02:39.482
Comfortable, but not confident:

45
00:02:39.762 --> 00:02:44.690
Skim Phase 1 and do only the exercises, then start properly with Phase 2.

46
00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.378
Experienced professional:

47
00:02:46.658 --> 00:02:48.173
Jump to the phase you need:

48
00:02:48.453 --> 00:02:51.162
Phase 4, Workplace or Phase 5, Career.

49
00:02:52.512 --> 00:02:53.195
Quote:

50
00:02:53.475 --> 00:02:56.312
Soft skills are hard skills you practise out loud..

51
00:02:56.592 --> 00:02:58.384
Confident speakers aren't born.

52
00:02:58.664 --> 00:03:04.104
They have prepared phrases, they practise them out loud, and they reflect on every conversation.

53
00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:07.648
This course gives you all three, 20 to 30 minutes a day.

54
00:03:08.998 --> 00:03:10.534
That's the end of this lesson.

55
00:03:10.814 --> 00:03:15.465
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

56
00:03:15.745 --> 00:03:21.867
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

